# sherpa-onnx v1.13.7 prebuilt static-link archives (k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx GitHub Releases:
# https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/v1.13.7/<filename>).
#
# sherpa-onnx-sys's build.rs does NOT verify these hashes itself (Step 0 finding, 2026-09) —
# this file is our own supply-chain check. Consumed by scripts/fetch-sherpa-archive.sh, which
# .github/workflows/release.yml, ci.yml, and packaging/build_windows.ps1 / build_dmg.sh all
# call before pointing SHERPA_ONNX_ARCHIVE_DIR at the download.
#
# Bump this file together with the `sherpa-onnx = "=X.Y.Z"` pin in stt/Cargo.toml — a minor
# version drift changes build.rs's download URL and swaps the whole prebuilt archive set.
#
# The size column is informational (it is what a caller should expect to download; note the
# Windows archive is six times the others, because its ONNX Runtime static lib alone is 916 MB).
# It is a third field on purpose: fetch-sherpa-archive.sh reads fields with awk and only looks
# at the first two. (`sha256sum -c` would take the rest of the line as the file name, so strip
# the size first: awk '!/^#/ && NF {print $1 "  " $2}' … | sha256sum -c -)
#
# <sha256>  <filename>  <bytes>
